      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1356",
      "html": "<ul><li>Scientific name: Plotosus canius Hamilton, 1822</li><li>Type locality: Southern Bengal, India.</li><li>Identification: a plain dusky-brown species with a black dorsal fin tip. It shows a banded pattern at night. It is distinguished from adult Plotosus lineatus by its long nostril barbels, which can reach past the eyes.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1356",
      "html": "<p>Indo-West Pacific: west and south coasts of India and off Sri Lanka, eastward along the coasts of Bangladesh and Myanmar, through the Indo-Australian Archipelago and the Philippines as far as Papua New Guinea.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1356",
      "html": "<p>A brackish water to marine species.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1356",
      "html": "<p>Unreported. There is no breeding report.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1356",
      "html": "<p>The spines associated with the anterior fins have potent venom.</p>"
    },
